Metadata-Version: 2.1
Name: ytauto-it-stages
Version: 0.0.0
Summary: Entry-point metadata for the integration suite's synthetic stages.

This directory is hand-written distribution metadata, not an installed
package. ``importlib.metadata`` discovers entry points by scanning every
``sys.path`` entry for ``*.dist-info`` directories, and the integration
fixtures already put ``tests/`` on ``sys.path`` (and on the ``PYTHONPATH`` a
worker subprocess inherits) so that a worker can import the synthetic stage
modules at all. Registering them here rather than in the project's own
``pyproject.toml`` has three points in its favour:

1. The shipped ``ytauto`` distribution does not advertise stages that live in
   the test tree and would fail to import for anyone who installed it.
2. No ``pip install -e .`` is needed for a test-only stage, so the suite
   cannot silently run against stale entry-point metadata.
3. It is the real third-party plugin path, exercised end to end: a *separate*
   distribution registering ``ytauto.stages`` entry points is exactly how a
   provider package will ship, and the integration suite now proves that
   works across a process boundary instead of asserting it in prose.
